  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Mental Model & Sequence Rules",
      "items": [
        "Loading creates the InstanceKlass in native Metaspace; Linking validates structure and prepares slots; Initialization runs <clinit>",
        "Preparation sets specification default values (0, null); user static initializers do NOT run until Initialization",
        "Compile-time constants (static final primitive/String) are populated during Preparation via ConstantValue attributes",
        "Only Initialization executes user Java code; all earlier phases construct and validate metadata"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Metaspace vs Java Heap",
      "items": [
        "InstanceKlass, vtables, and static field slots reside in Metaspace (native RAM outside -Xmx)",
        "Class<T> mirror object and static heap references (e.g. int[] array instances) live on the Java Heap",
        "Runtime Constant Pool entries remain symbolic text until lazily resolved into direct 64-bit memory addresses on first instruction use",
        "Metaspace exhaustion (OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace) can occur from dynamic proxies even while Java Heap is completely empty"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Interview Traps & Edge Cases",
      "items": [
        "VerifyError: Bytecode structural proof failure (almost always stale agent transforms, ASM version mismatch, or corrupted StackMapTable)",
        "ExceptionInInitializerError: Escaped exception marks class permanently erroneous; subsequent touches throw causeless NoClassDefFoundError",
        "Circular static initialization: Re-entrant threads proceed on half-initialized classes, observing default null/0 values without exceptions",
        "Holder idiom is completely thread-safe without synchronized because HotSpot serializes execution under the class initialization lock"
      ]
    }
  ]
